.TH OLLAMA\-MESH 1 "2026-08-17" "ollama-mesh dev" "ollama-mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
ollama\-mesh \- CLI client for the ollama\-mesh Admin API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ollama\-mesh
.I command
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ollama\-mesh is a single static binary that is three tools in one - the mesh server, a Node Agent, and this thin CLI client of the Admin API - selected by the first argument. As a CLI, every subcommand below is exactly one Admin API request; it never talks to a Node Agent directly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
print CLI and (if reachable) server version
.TP
.B status
print mesh health/status summary
.TP
.B login
authenticate once and save the session locally (recommended)
.TP
.B logout
remove the saved session
.TP
.B whoami
show the CLI's saved identity (live\-verified)
.TP
.B nodes
list nodes known to the mesh. See \fBollama-mesh-nodes\fR(1).
.TP
.B models
fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node. See \fBollama-mesh-models\fR(1).
.TP
.B runtime
start/stop/restart/logs/drain/undrain/health on one node. See \fBollama-mesh-runtime\fR(1).
.TP
.B node
node control driver operations. See \fBollama-mesh-node\fR(1).
.TP
.B key
per\-API-key local/cloud routing overrides. See \fBollama-mesh-key\fR(1).
.TP
.B spill
show per\-key, per\-provider local\-vs-cloud request counts
.TP
.B requests
inspect routing decisions for past requests. See \fBollama-mesh-requests\fR(1).
.TP
.B completion <shell>
generate a shell completion script (bash, zsh, or fish)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MESH_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MESH_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MESH_PASSWORD)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User error (bad arguments, unknown command, validation failure).
.TP
.B 2
Server error (the Admin API is unreachable or returned an unexpected error).
.TP
.B 3
Reserved for future partial-success reporting (batch operations); unused today.
.TP
.B 4
Authentication error (missing, invalid, or expired credentials).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MESH_SERVER
Admin API base URL, used when \-\-server is not given.
.TP
.B MESH_USERNAME
Admin username, used when \-\-username is not given.
.TP
.B MESH_PASSWORD
Admin password, used when \-\-password is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ollama-mesh/session
The session saved by "ollama\-mesh login" (mode 0600), under the OS user config dir - e.g. ~/.config/ollama\-mesh/session on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support/ollama\-mesh/session on macOS, %AppData%\eollama\-mesh\esession on Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
source <(ollama\-mesh completion bash)
.fi
.PP
.nf
ollama\-mesh completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_ollama\-mesh"
.fi
.PP
.nf
ollama\-mesh completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/ollama\-mesh.fish
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBollama-mesh-nodes\fR(1),
\fBollama-mesh-models\fR(1),
\fBollama-mesh-runtime\fR(1),
\fBollama-mesh-node\fR(1),
\fBollama-mesh-key\fR(1),
\fBollama-mesh-requests\fR(1)
